= Courses at Northwestern

I teach courses in statistics, machine learning, and generative AI at Northwestern University.

- *IEMS 490: Deep Generative AI* (with a focus on diffusion and flow models), Winter 2026
    -- [notes0.pdf 1. Discriminative and Generative Models]
    -- [notes1.pdf 2. Mathematical Background]
    -- [notes2.pdf 3. VAEs and Diffusion Models] | [implementation.pdf Implementation Details]
    -- [notes3.pdf 4. Efficient Sampling: DDIM and Consistency Models]
    -- [notes4.pdf 5. Continuous-Time Formulation of Diffusion Models]
    -- [notes5.pdf 6. Conditional Diffusion Models] | [reward_guidance.pptx Slides: Reward Guidance]
    -- [notes6.pdf 7. Diffusion Models and Reinforcement Learning] | [VLA.pptx Slides: Vision-Language-Action Models]
    -- [notes7.pdf 8. Flow Matching]

- *IEMS 401: Applied Mathematical Statistics*, Fall 2024, Fall 2025

- *IEMS 304: Statistical Learning for Data Analysis*, Winter 2025, Winter 2026
